      "value": "@{5e5eaad1d85884539b238412|full_name}: \n\nThanks for sharing your verification results. It suggested that the relatively new World SDK may contain the problem.\n\nThe problem was reproduced even on my world updated with the latest SDK, i.e. 3.2.3.\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_6fecf18a-ab96-43f2-82dc-ccf79f17c34f\n\nNow, the following is pure speculation, but it is common practice to lower the volume setting of the Audio Source component in Unity below the default value of 1.0 when the original audio file is excessively loud. The problem you describe seems similar to what happens when Volume is overridden to 1.0 during world initialization.\n\nThere may be a bug in the latest world SDK for VRChat_Quest that causes such scripts to run during world initialization.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
